From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pkg-config: export includedir as a variable

The .pc file already substitutes @includedir@ into Cflags, but exposes
only prefix as a queryable variable. A consumer that wants the path to
gdesktop-enums.h - gnome-control-center does, to feed it to
gnome.mkenums_simple() - therefore has to build it from prefix:

    gsettings_desktop_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig: 'prefix')
        + '/include/gsettings-desktop-schemas/gdesktop-enums.h'

which is wrong under a sysroot: cross pkg-config prefixes includedir
and libdir with the sysroot but leaves prefix alone, so the result
points at the build machine's /usr/include and the file is not there.

Export includedir as a variable so consumers can ask for the thing
they actually want.

Upstream: not yet submitted, will go to
https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gsettings-desktop-schemas/-/merge_requests
Signed-off-by: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
--- a/gsettings-desktop-schemas.pc.in
+++ b/gsettings-desktop-schemas.pc.in
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 prefix=@prefix@
+includedir=@includedir@
 
 Name: gsettings-desktop-schemas
 Description: Shared GSettings schemas for the desktop, including helper headers
